items.why:
Done as asked. Both rules are in index.html verbatim from the C6h gate's text, each once, at lines 1479-1480. They work as the gate tested:
- at 412-413, one-line names are 17 px with 3.5 px gaps, which passes the spacing exception at zero margin by boxes;
- at 414-441, one-line names are 24 px and two-line names 34 px;
- all four names are whole from 412, as on OLD, and no name is less visible at any square.

By box geometry 2.5.8 now fails at no whole name. It fails at 45 squares, all cut names (352-368, 371-393, 407-411), against OLD's 75, which include whole names at 412-441. This holds with overlay and with classic 15 px scrollbars.

Caveat (HC-2): by the region that really takes a tap, 'Tropos in Acid' (412-441) and 'Core in Ember' (412-428) are still 1-2 px short. That is not worse than OLD.

Squares outside 412-441 and 463-504 are identical in every measured field, and inside them only the names' boxes and text positions change. The picture, headline, line, buttons, left edges, dots and header clearance are identical at all 1,081 squares.

Non-square windows are identical in every field:
- all 3,025 grid windows (320-1400 x 300-1400, step 20);
- 1,602 near-squares (within 1 %, including 74 between 999/1000 and 1001/1000);
- 113 real-device windows (phones upright and sideways, tablets, desktops);
- the five named devices: 390x844, 375x667, 768x1024, 1440x900, 1366x768.

Tab stops and scrollY from the top are identical at 16 windows. There were 0 page errors in 15,314 measurements.

Confirmed:
- only the 45 HTML pages and site_fix.py change (git diff f0e265013e..b50849e568: 46 files);
- vercel.json and robots.txt are unchanged, and 'noindex, nofollow' stays;
- the CSS rules are verbatim;
- 2.5.8 fails at no whole name, by boxes (see HC-2);
- no name is less visible, and the whole names match C6h at every square;
- Tropos is whole at 463-504 under the override;
- C6i-3 costs no name.

Corrected: the 412-413 cost under the override is real but not load-order dependent in eight orders tested. Its numbers are 43.5-46.6 % of the text against 49.7-51.7 % (23-24 of 42 px against 26-26.7 of 44 px by box). The 71 % did not reproduce.

